Based on the provided excerpts, to make a character jump when the player presses the "jump" action and the character is on the floor, you instantly give them a lot of vertical speed [1]. 

In GDScript, this is implemented by setting the vertical velocity:
```gdscript
if Input.is_action_just_pressed("jump"):
    velocity.y = JUMP_SPEED
```
*(Note: For CharacterBody2D, it also checks `is_on_floor()`)* [2, 4].

In C#, this is implemented as:
```csharp
if (Input.IsActionJustPressed("jump"))
    {
        Velocity = Vector3.Up * JumpSpeed;
    }
```
